1. What you may do
  a. Play: download, build, install and run the Software on your own devices,
     and record, stream and share videos and screenshots of it (monetized or
     not), as long as you do not present the Software as made by anyone other
     than the Owner.
  b. Make content: create mods, charts, songs, scripts, characters, stages and
     other content that runs in the Software, and share it however you like.
     Your content is yours, as long as it does not contain the Software's
     code.
  c. Collaborate: fork the official repository on GitHub and change the
     source code to prepare contributions to it (pull requests, patches,
     issues). A fork must keep this License, the copyright notice and the
     credits, and must say that it is a fork of the official repository.
  d. Read the source code and learn from it.

2. What needs the Owner's written permission
  Unless the Owner has given you written permission (section 3), you may not:
  a. publish, share or distribute the Software or a modified version of it,
     as source code or as builds, anywhere other than the official
     repository, its official releases and GitHub forks used as section 1c
     allows;
  b. publish a modified version of the Software, or a program built from its
     code, as a separate project or engine, under any name;
  c. remove or change the copyright notice, this License or the credits, or
     present the Software or any part of it as your own work, or name
     yourself as its author or co-author;
  d. sell the Software or a modified version of it, or charge for access to
     either;
  e. use the names "God's Hand of Principality and Demise" or "God's Hand" for
     another project, other than to say that it is based on the Software.

3. Collaborators
  The Owner can give written permission for anything listed in section 2
  (for example, to publish a fork under its own name with its own releases)
  in an issue, discussion or pull request of the official repository, or in
  a file there. A person or project with such permission is a Collaborator.
  The permission covers only what it says, and a Collaborator must always
  credit the Software as "Based on God's Hand of Principality and Demise by
  deatuamae67-crypto", with a link to the official repository.

4. Contributions
  When you send a contribution to the official repository (a pull request, a
  patch, or code in an issue), you agree that the Owner may include it in the
  Software and publish it under this License or any later license the Owner
  chooses. You keep the copyright of your contribution and stay credited as
  its author in the repository's history.

5. Mods and mod packs
  The mod packs published on the "mods" release are not part of the Software
  and are not covered by this License. Not all of them are the Owner's: some
  were made by the Owner, and the others belong to their original creators,
  who keep every right to them. They are shared so they can be played in
  God's Hand.

